    emend probe links `quick-xml` yet.
    
    The editing probe is larger than the no-edit one by 65140
    section bytes (50672 of `.text`) and by 65536
    file bytes, for two reasons, separated by a third build that edits but reads
    no entry:
    
    | Part | Section bytes | .text bytes | File bytes |
    | --- | --- | --- | --- |
    | the edit paths, which a consumer that never edits lets the linker drop | 2600 | 1936 | 0 |
    | reading an entry through the layer (`Archive::read` goes through `zip`) | 62540 | 48736 | 65536 |
    
    Reading is most of the difference. A consumer that reads entries links it
    whether or not it edits.
    
    ## The budget
    
    The provisional budget is 250 KiB, 256000 bytes, above `probe-zip-xml`.
    Judged on `probe-emend-edit`: 118784 file bytes and 116088 section
    bytes, leaving 137216 and 139912. The
    maintainer re-rules the budget with these figures in hand.
    
    ## Reading these figures
    
    File sizes on this target change in whole 4096-byte steps. They are not
    themselves whole pages: all four probes leave the same remainder, 2596 bytes,
    modulo 4096, so it is every DIFFERENCE between them that is a whole number of
    pages. A change under a page is therefore invisible in the file size, and a
    change of a few bytes can cost a page: the committed duplicate check costs
    5016 section bytes and 8192 file bytes in `probe-emend-edit`. The section
    totals, from `size -A`, resolve to the byte, which is why both are given.
    
    ## The duplicate-name candidates
    
    `refuse_duplicate_names` was quadratic in P2 and is linear-logarithmic from
    Milestone 1 part 1 P3. Each form below was built from a clone of this commit
    differing only in that function.
    
    | Form | `probe-emend-copy` sections | `probe-emend-edit` sections |
